1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,847
This is a 78-ton passenger jet.

2
00:00:02,847 --> 00:00:06,850
In about 40 seconds, it will leave the ground.

3
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:08,773
Trick one: thrust.

4
00:00:08,773 --> 00:00:14,091
Two turbofan engines swallow air and blast it out the back.

5
00:00:14,091 --> 00:00:19,950
By Newton's third law, the jet surges forward, to about 270 km/h.

6
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,469
Trick two: lift.

7
00:00:21,469 --> 00:00:24,668
The wing is curved and tilted slightly up.

8
00:00:24,668 --> 00:00:31,903
Air over the top speeds up and its pressure drops, while the wing pushes the air below it down.

9
00:00:31,903 --> 00:00:34,950
That pressure difference lifts the wing.

10
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:38,281
At rotation speed, the pilot pulls back.

11
00:00:38,281 --> 00:00:44,950
The nose rises about ten degrees, flaps add extra lift, and the wheels leave the runway.

12
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,933
The catch: lift grows with the square of speed.

13
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:52,694
Half the speed gives only a quarter of the lift.

14
00:00:52,694 --> 00:00:55,750
That's why runways are kilometers long.

15
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:57,622
Engines to move.

16
00:00:57,622 --> 00:00:58,900
Wings to fly.

17
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:01,750
That's how a plane takes off.
